  "raw_text": "Step 1: First, we need to find the value of \\( q(1) \\). Given that \\( q(x) = bx + 1 \\), we substitute \\( x = 1 \\) into the function \\( q(x) \\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate \\( q(1) \\):\n\\[ q(1) = b(1) + 1 = b + 1 \\]\n\nStep 3: Now, we use the given information that \\( f(q(1)) = -3 \\). We know \\( f(x) = x - 3 \\), so we substitute \\( q(1) \\) into \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ f(q(1)) = f(b + 1) = (b + 1) - 3 \\]\n\nStep 4: Set the expression from Step 3 equal to \\(-3\\) and solve for \\( b \\):\n\\[ (b + 1) - 3 = -3 \\]\n\\[ b + 1 - 3 = -3 \\]\n\\[ b - 2 = -3 \\]\n\\[ b = -3 + 2 \\]\n\\[ b = -1 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-1}<|im_end|>",
